{title: Live at peace}
{subtitle: Romans 12:17–18}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | ×9

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Repay no one evil for evil
Give careful thought to what is honorable
Do not be wise in your own [Bb]eyes
Associate [Ab]with the lowly, stay [Eb]humble
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
If [Cm]it is possible, as far as it depends [Ab]on you
Live at [Eb]peace with everyone
Do not [Bb]be overcome by evil
O[Ab]vercome evil with [Eb]good
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Bless those who persecute you
Bless [Cm]them and do not curse them
Rejoice [Eb]with those who rejoice
[Bb]Weep with those who [Ab]weep, be one [Eb]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
If [Cm]it is possible, as far as it depends [Ab]on you
Live at [Eb]peace with everyone
Do not [Bb]be overcome by evil
[Ab]Overcome evil [Eb]with good
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] |
| [Cm] | [Cm] | [Ab] | [Ab] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | ×2

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
If your [Eb]enemy is hungry, feed him
If he [Cm]is thirsty, give him something to drink
You will heap [Eb]burning coals on his head
[Bb]Leave room for God's [Ab]wrath, dear [Eb]friends
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
If [Cm]it is possible, as far as it depends [Ab]on you
Live at [Eb]peace with everyone
Do not [Bb]be overcome by evil
O[Ab]vercome e[Eb]vil with good
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Vengeance is mine, I will re[Ab]pay
Says the Lord, [Eb]the only judge
Do not [Cm]take revenge, dear friends
[Bb]Trust in His per[Ab]fect, holy [Eb]love
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Live at [Bb]peace with everyone
Overcome [Ab]evil with [Eb]good
{end_of_verse}
